<txp:hide>
  with — hands its attributes to every form called inside it. Outputs only its contents.

  <txp::with article_headline="h0-style" article_figure="a_image--fold-limited">
    <txp:article form="super" />
  </txp::with>

  Values reach EVERY form nested inside, not just the one you mean, so:
  - prefix each name with the family of forms it's for: article_… (default, super),
    thumb_… (thumb, thumb_super). Forms in one family share names, so you can swap
    form="super" for form="default" (or thumb for thumb_super) without touching the page.
  - never pass a plain name (class, id, limit, offset, category…): figure, gallery,
    m_embed, o_footer and others read those, and would pick them up.
  - yield's default="…" only applies when x isn't passed at all; x="" gives empty.
    To test "set and not empty", use if_yield with a bare value attribute: name="x" value
    (Tags in this note must be balanced, or TXP reports an unclosed tag: hence no brackets.)
</txp:hide>
<txp:yield />